## Redux Toolkit + RTK Query - State Management Rules

### Core Principles
- **Redux Toolkit** for global application state (user auth, UI state, settings)
- **RTK Query** for all API calls (automatic caching, loading states, refetching)
- **Custom hooks** for feature business logic (orchestrate RTK Query + local state)
- **Utility hooks** for reusable patterns (debounce, pagination, notifications)

### Redux Folder Structure

```
src/
├── store/                          # Core Redux setup
│   ├── api/
│   │   └── apiSlice.ts            # Base RTK Query API configuration
│   ├── slices/
│   │   └── appSlice.ts            # Global app state (notifications, loading)
│   ├── hooks.ts                    # Typed Redux hooks (useAppDispatch, useAppSelector)
│   ├── store.ts                    # Store configuration
│   └── StoreProvider.tsx           # Next.js provider wrapper
│
├── features/{feature}/
│   ├── api/
│   │   ├── {feature}Api.ts        # RTK Query endpoints for this feature
│   │   └── index.ts               # Re-exports
│   ├── hooks/
│   │   ├── use{Feature}.ts        # Business logic hook
│   │   └── index.ts               # Re-exports
│   └── models/
│       └── {feature}.ts           # API types/interfaces
│
└── hooks/                          # Shared utility hooks
    ├── useDebounce.ts
    ├── usePagination.ts
    └── useNotification.ts
```

### Store Configuration Rules

#### 1. Base API Slice (`src/store/api/apiSlice.ts`)
```typescript
import { createApi, fetchBaseQuery } from "@reduxjs/toolkit/query/react";

const BASE_URL = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL || "http://localhost:3000/api";

export const apiSlice = createApi({
  reducerPath: "api",
  baseQuery: fetchBaseQuery({
    baseUrl: BASE_URL,
    prepareHeaders: (headers) => {
      // Add auth headers here
      headers.set("Content-Type", "application/json");
      return headers;
    },
  }),
  tagTypes: ["Feature1", "Feature2"], // Add cache tags here
  endpoints: () => ({}), // Features inject endpoints
});
```

#### 2. App Slice (`src/store/slices/appSlice.ts`)
```typescript
import { createSlice, PayloadAction } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";
import type { RootState } from "@/store/store";

interface AppState {
  isGlobalLoading: boolean;
  notification: { message: string; type: string; show: boolean } | null;
}

const initialState: AppState = {
  isGlobalLoading: false,
  notification: null,
};

export const appSlice = createSlice({
  name: "app",
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    setGlobalLoading: (state, action: PayloadAction<boolean>) => {
      state.isGlobalLoading = action.payload;
    },
    // ... other reducers
  },
});

export const { setGlobalLoading } = appSlice.actions;
export const selectGlobalLoading = (state: RootState) => state.app.isGlobalLoading;
export default appSlice.reducer;
```

#### 3. Store Setup (`src/store/store.ts`)
```typescript
import { configureStore } from "@reduxjs/toolkit";
import { apiSlice } from "./api/apiSlice";
import appReducer from "./slices/appSlice";

export const makeStore = () => {
  return configureStore({
    reducer: {
      app: appReducer,
      [apiSlice.reducerPath]: apiSlice.reducer,
      // Add feature slices here
    },
    middleware: (getDefaultMiddleware) =>
      getDefaultMiddleware().concat(apiSlice.middleware),
  });
};

export type AppStore = ReturnType<typeof makeStore>;
export type RootState = ReturnType<AppStore["getState"]>;
export type AppDispatch = AppStore["dispatch"];
```

#### 4. Typed Hooks (`src/store/hooks.ts`)
```typescript
import { useDispatch, useSelector, useStore } from "react-redux";
import type { AppDispatch, AppStore, RootState } from "@/store/store";

export const useAppDispatch = useDispatch.withTypes<AppDispatch>();
export const useAppSelector = useSelector.withTypes<RootState>();
export const useAppStore = useStore.withTypes<AppStore>();
```

#### 5. Provider (`src/store/StoreProvider.tsx`)
```typescript
"use client";
import { useRef } from "react";
import { Provider } from "react-redux";
import { makeStore, AppStore } from "./store";

export default function StoreProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  const storeRef = useRef<AppStore>();
  if (!storeRef.current) {
    storeRef.current = makeStore();
  }
  return <Provider store={storeRef.current}>{children}</Provider>;
}
```

### Feature API Pattern (RTK Query)

#### Creating Feature API (`features/{feature}/api/{feature}Api.ts`)
```typescript
import { apiSlice } from "@/store/api/apiSlice";
import type { Item, ItemFilters, ItemResponse } from "../models";

export const featureApi = apiSlice.injectEndpoints({
  endpoints: (builder) => ({
    // GET: Fetch items with filters
    getItems: builder.query<ItemResponse, ItemFilters>({
      query: (filters = {}) => {
        const params = new URLSearchParams();
        if (filters.page) params.append("page", String(filters.page));
        // Add other params
        return `/items?${params.toString()}`;
      },
      providesTags: (result) =>
        result
          ? [
              ...result.items.map(({ id }) => ({ type: "Item" as const, id })),
              { type: "Item", id: "LIST" },
            ]
          : [{ type: "Item", id: "LIST" }],
    }),

    // GET: Single item
    getItemById: builder.query<Item, string>({
      query: (id) => `/items/${id}`,
      providesTags: (result, error, id) => [{ type: "Item", id }],
    }),

    // POST: Create item (mutation)
    createItem: builder.mutation<Item, Partial<Item>>({
      query: (newItem) => ({
        url: "/items",
        method: "POST",
        body: newItem,
      }),
      invalidatesTags: [{ type: "Item", id: "LIST" }],
    }),

    // PATCH: Update item
    updateItem: builder.mutation<Item, { id: string; data: Partial<Item> }>({
      query: ({ id, data }) => ({
        url: `/items/${id}`,
        method: "PATCH",
        body: data,
      }),
      invalidatesTags: (result, error, { id }) => [
        { type: "Item", id },
        { type: "Item", id: "LIST" },
      ],
    }),

    // DELETE: Delete item
    deleteItem: builder.mutation<void, string>({
      query: (id) => ({
        url: `/items/${id}`,
        method: "DELETE",
      }),
      invalidatesTags: (result, error, id) => [
        { type: "Item", id },
        { type: "Item", id: "LIST" },
      ],
    }),
  }),
});

// Export auto-generated hooks
export const {
  useGetItemsQuery,
  useGetItemByIdQuery,
  useCreateItemMutation,
  useUpdateItemMutation,
  useDeleteItemMutation,
} = featureApi;
```

### Feature Hook Pattern (Business Logic)

#### Creating Feature Hook (`features/{feature}/hooks/use{Feature}.ts`)
```typescript
import { useState, useCallback, useMemo } from "react";
import { useDebounce } from "@/hooks/useDebounce";
import { usePagination } from "@/hooks/usePagination";
import { useNotification } from "@/hooks/useNotification";
import { useGetItemsQuery, useCreateItemMutation } from "../api/featureApi";

export const useFeature = () => {
  // 1. LOCAL STATE
  const [searchInput, setSearchInput] = useState("");
  const [filter, setFilter] = useState<string | undefined>();

  // 2. UTILITY HOOKS
  const { success, error: showError } = useNotification();
  const debouncedSearch = useDebounce(searchInput, 500);
  const pagination = usePagination({ defaultPerPage: 10 });

  // 3. BUILD QUERY PARAMS
  const filters = useMemo(() => ({
    page: pagination.currentPage,
    perPage: pagination.itemsPerPage,
    search: debouncedSearch || undefined,
    filter,
  }), [pagination.currentPage, pagination.itemsPerPage, debouncedSearch, filter]);

  // 4. RTK QUERY HOOKS
  const { data, isLoading, isFetching } = useGetItemsQuery(filters);
  const [createItem, { isLoading: isCreating }] = useCreateItemMutation();

  // 5. COMPUTED VALUES
  const items = useMemo(() => data?.items || [], [data?.items]);
  const totalPages = useMemo(() => data?.totalPages || 1, [data?.totalPages]);

  // 6. EVENT HANDLERS
  const handleSearchChange = useCallback((e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {
    setSearchInput(e.target.value);
    pagination.setCurrentPage(1);
  }, [pagination]);

  const handleCreate = useCallback(async (itemData: any) => {
    try {
      await createItem(itemData).unwrap();
      success("Item created successfully");
      return { success: true };
    } catch (error) {
      showError("Failed to create item");
      return { success: false };
    }
  }, [createItem, success, showError]);

  // 7. RETURN API
  return {
    // Data
    items,
    totalPages,
    currentPage: pagination.currentPage,
    // Loading
    isLoading,
    isFetching,
    isCreating,
    // Search & Filters
    searchInput,
    filter,
    handleSearchChange,
    setFilter,
    // Pagination
    handlePageChange: pagination.handlePageChange,
    // Actions
    handleCreate,
  };
};
```

### Utility Hooks

#### useDebounce
```typescript
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";

export function useDebounce<T>(value: T, delay: number = 500): T {
  const [debouncedValue, setDebouncedValue] = useState<T>(value);

  useEffect(() => {
    const handler = setTimeout(() => setDebouncedValue(value), delay);
    return () => clearTimeout(handler);
  }, [value, delay]);

  return debouncedValue;
}
```

#### usePagination
```typescript
import { useState, useCallback } from "react";

export function usePagination({ defaultPage = 1, defaultPerPage = 10 } = {}) {
  const [currentPage, setCurrentPage] = useState(defaultPage);
  const [itemsPerPage, setItemsPerPage] = useState(defaultPerPage);

  const handlePageChange = useCallback((page: number) => {
    setCurrentPage(page);
  }, []);

  const handleItemsPerPageChange = useCallback((perPage: number) => {
    setItemsPerPage(perPage);
    setCurrentPage(1);
  }, []);

  const resetPagination = useCallback(() => {
    setCurrentPage(defaultPage);
    setItemsPerPage(defaultPerPage);
  }, [defaultPage, defaultPerPage]);

  return {
    currentPage,
    itemsPerPage,
    setCurrentPage,
    setItemsPerPage,
    handlePageChange,
    handleItemsPerPageChange,
    resetPagination,
  };
}
```

#### useNotification
```typescript
import { useCallback } from "react";
import { useAppDispatch } from "@/store/hooks";
import { showNotification, hideNotification } from "@/store/slices/appSlice";

export function useNotification() {
  const dispatch = useAppDispatch();

  const success = useCallback((message: string) => {
    dispatch(showNotification({ message, type: "success" }));
  }, [dispatch]);

  const error = useCallback((message: string) => {
    dispatch(showNotification({ message, type: "error" }));
  }, [dispatch]);

  const info = useCallback((message: string) => {
    dispatch(showNotification({ message, type: "info" }));
  }, [dispatch]);

  const hide = useCallback(() => {
    dispatch(hideNotification());
  }, [dispatch]);

  return { success, error, info, hide };
}
```

### Usage in Components

#### Using Feature Hook (Recommended)
```typescript
"use client";
import { useFeature } from "@/features/myfeature/hooks";

export default function MyFeaturePage() {
  const {
    items,
    isLoading,
    searchInput,
    handleSearchChange,
    currentPage,
    totalPages,
    handlePageChange,
    handleCreate,
  } = useFeature();

  return (
    <div>
      <input value={searchInput} onChange={handleSearchChange} />
      {isLoading ? <Loading /> : <ItemsList items={items} />}
      <Pagination current={currentPage} total={totalPages} onChange={handlePageChange} />
    </div>
  );
}
```

#### Using Direct RTK Query Hook (Simple Cases)
```typescript
"use client";
import { useGetItemsQuery } from "@/features/myfeature/api";

export default function SimpleList() {
  const { data, isLoading } = useGetItemsQuery({ page: 1, perPage: 10 });

  if (isLoading) return <Loading />;
  return <ItemsList items={data?.items} />;
}
```

### Redux Rules Summary

#### DO
- **Always use typed hooks** (`useAppDispatch`, `useAppSelector`, not plain Redux hooks)
- **Create feature APIs** by injecting endpoints into `apiSlice`
- **Use RTK Query** for all API calls (queries and mutations)
- **Create custom feature hooks** to orchestrate RTK Query + local state + business logic
- **Use utility hooks** for common patterns (debounce, pagination, notifications)
- **Memoize computed values** with `useMemo`
- **Memoize callbacks** with `useCallback` when passed to children or used in deps
- **Use cache tags** properly for automatic refetching (`providesTags`, `invalidatesTags`)
- **Keep components thin** - all logic in hooks
- **Follow folder structure exactly** (api/, hooks/, models/ in features/)
- **Export from index.ts** for clean imports

#### DON'T
- **Don't use plain Redux hooks** (`useDispatch`, `useSelector` without types)
- **Don't fetch with fetch/axios** - always use RTK Query
- **Don't put business logic in components** - use custom hooks
- **Don't hardcode API URLs** - use `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` env variable
- **Don't skip cache tags** - they enable automatic refetching
- **Don't create multiple hooks per feature** - one public hook that orchestrates everything
- **Don't mix API logic with component logic**
- **Don't forget to add new tag types** to `apiSlice` tagTypes array
- **Don't create duplicate state** - if RTK Query has it, use it

#### Integration Checklist
When adding Redux to a new feature:
1. ✅ Create `features/{feature}/api/{feature}Api.ts` with endpoints
2. ✅ Add cache tags to `store/api/apiSlice.ts` tagTypes
3. ✅ Create types in `features/{feature}/models/{feature}.ts`
4. ✅ Create `features/{feature}/hooks/use{Feature}.ts` hook
5. ✅ Export from `api/index.ts` and `hooks/index.ts`
6. ✅ Use feature hook in components
7. ✅ Test queries and mutations work
8. ✅ Verify caching and refetching behavior

#### Environment Setup
- Create `.env.local` with `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=your-api-url`
- API calls will automatically use this base URL
- Auth headers can be added in `apiSlice.ts` prepareHeaders

#### File Naming
- API files: `{feature}Api.ts` (e.g., `userApi.ts`, `productApi.ts`)
- Hooks: `use{Feature}.ts` (e.g., `useUser.ts`, `useProduct.ts`)
- Models: `{feature}.ts` (e.g., `user.ts`, `product.ts`)

By following these Redux rules, you ensure consistent, maintainable, and scalable state management across the entire application.s